    "description": "Railroad programming is a functional programming paradigm that manages flow control, especially success vs failure, without messy if/else chains or exceptions everywhere.\n\nThe image comes from the sequence of step, expressed as a train track: one rail links the different successes, while the other rail links all the failures. It is possible to go from success to failure. ",
